      "body": [
        "LiteLLM lets applications call different model providers through a common interface; OpenInference records those calls for investigation. Its Python LiteLLM instrumentation version 0.1.51 fixes several cases where a span, the record of one operation inside a trace, could remain open or lose useful evidence. The release covers failed calls, unread streams and responses that end without completing normally. It also records partial output when a stream closes early.",
        "For illustration, a user could stop an assistant after the first few words. The relevant debugging record should still show what arrived before cancellation. The linked fix explains that output attributes were previously written only after the stream loop completed, leaving early-closed streams without those attributes. Another fix marks mid-stream failures with ERROR status, making them visible to views and alerts that filter by status.",
        "The notes also address forwarding a wrapper’s close call to the underlying stream and keeping the span current while streaming calls run. Maintainer tests support these specific paths; they are not a guarantee for every provider or application lifecycle. Operators should exercise cancellation, unread responses and interrupted connections in their own integration."
